    "collateral_ratio_basis": "apyUSD is a wrapper: it holds apxUSD, so its backing ratio IS apxUSD's issuer-attested collateralization, netted on both sides \u2014 (reserves - POL - inventory) / (supply - POL - inventory). A claim on apxUSD is worth what apxUSD is backed by. \u26a0\ufe0f NOT comparable to a gross collateral ratio. \u26a0\ufe0f The share-vs-assets ratio is NOT used here: nav is defined as total_assets/shares, so assets/(shares x nav) is 100.0% by construction and cannot fail. It is published as share_coverage_tautological_pct with that label rather than rated.",
    "axis_rating_basis": "Rated on the generic band deliberately \u2014 no anchor exists in this analyzer, and the apparent agreement between the axis (2/5) and the published backing score (2.0/10) is COINCIDENTAL. The axis rates coverage; the score rates basket composition (~74% STRC) and dislocation, which a collateral ratio cannot express. Expect them to diverge when STRC moves without the CR moving \u2014 that is the design, not a defect.",
